# `@Element` written without its element is refused by the checker (Semantics ch. 8:
# `@Element: fn Element r o -> @o emit r`), as a line and as a supplier's answer, so the
# back end's guard (lower/expr.prism, "`@Element` without its element") is not reached.
# Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

@child: @unit
@child:
    Ui.Label($text=$"child")

@page: @unit
@page:
    @Element
    ignore <- @HostDocument @child, \|p, e| @Element
